<title>AUSTRALIA: Lion Selection shares list at discount.</title>
<headline>Lion Selection shares list at discount.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in resources investment group Lion Selection Group Ltd made their debut on the Australian Stock Exchange on Thursday at 95 cents, a five cent discount to its A$1.00 issue price.</p>
<p>The company plans to operate as a pooled development fund which can provide taxation advantages, specialising in small to medium sized Australian resource companies which have gold or metals projects in Australia, Africa, South East Asia or India.</p>
<p>By 12.40 p.m. (0240 GMT), Lion shares were trading at 94 cents with 43,000 shares traded.</p>
<p>--Walter Watson, Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1810</p>
